      "keyFindings": [
        "In several of its model updates, Brooks has decreased the drop by a couple of mm, including the Glycerin 23 - a shift moving away from high-drop (10-12mm) running shoes and towards better gait efficiency.",
        "It has supercritical foams but is quite heavy with a pleasantly plush ride that struggles to move along, The fit is quite voluminous with some knit stretch in the mix upfront affecting hold for medium to narrow feet there when Brooks also has wides available.",
        "At $175, it is only an average value if plush luxurious riding is not your highest priority as there are several daily training alternatives at its price point and below with lighter weights and snappier rides, including Brooks Ghost 17 and Hyperion 3."
